From 94c36113667be7cf9358c3dedfbdca424df59245 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:01:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0308-port-sweetcpu-processor-boot.patch

port: xnu-11417 boots CPUs through processor_boot(). processor_start()
from IOKit is now a no-op returning KERN_FAILURE (Unsupported.exports
aliases it to processor_start_from_kext), and without USE_APPLEARMSMP
ml_processor_register() calls processor_boot() itself, while SweetCPU::start
is still registering that CPU. The generic boards keep SweetCPU's order
instead (register all, then boot CPU 0..n and wait for each), as
AppleARMSMP's cpu_boot_thread does: ml_processor_register leaves booting
to SweetCPU::startAll, which calls processor_boot() in place of
processor_start(). First boot of the 11417 kernel panicked with
"SWEET CPU: cpu=0 processor_start failed".
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp  | 25 ++++++++++---------------
 osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
index c37d05c0..1ab9e420 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
@@ -1789,8 +1789,11 @@ ml_processor_register(ml_processor_info_t *in_processor_info,
 
 	os_atomic_or(&this_cpu_datap->cpu_flags, InitState, relaxed);
 
-#if !USE_APPLEARMSMP
+#if !USE_APPLEARMSMP && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE)
 	/*
+	 * sweet: SweetCPU::startAll boots the CPUs itself, once all are
+	 * registered and in logical order (as AppleARMSMP does).
+	 *
 	 * AppleARMCPU's external processor_start call is now a no-op, so
 	 * boot the processor directly when it's registered.
 	 *
-- 
